CHANGE 4685180 MERGED 2023-07-26 17:54:10.000000000 91972744ac3601e2f628c8b6d5c40a4f31dae3f6 
sys-libs/llvm-libunwind: Remove ChromeOS workaround

Now that cmake-multilib.eclass has been updated (crrev/c/4622029), it
now defaults to using cmake.eclass instead of cmake-utils.eclass. As a
result, we can remove this workaround.

BUG=none
TEST=CQ passes

Change-Id: If4bc90365a5ea793ba1bbcc51220b62cac1537a6
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay/+/4685180
Auto-Submit: Matt Turner <msturner@google.com>
Tested-by: Matt Turner <msturner@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Matt Turner <msturner@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Jordan Abrahams-Whitehead <ajordanr@google.com>

CHANGE 4677913 MERGED 2023-07-12 15:38:45.000000000 f0894a0a76231c7f290537306f86c770190e3046 
glibc: stop using llvm-libunwind if it's installed

At the moment, the toolchain CQ is broken since cross-*/llvm-libunwind
is brought in earlier than it used to be (it's now installed during
chroot init, rather than some crossdev invocation). Since glibc seems to
build fine without automatic `--sysroot` application, we can disable
that for the glibc ebuild.

BUG=b:290144273
TEST=armv7a's `crossdev` command completes successfully

